--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
rp_ridge must reproduce the exp16 bar (ImageNet-R T=10 s0 R=32: 80.28) whenever
   NROWS=0; if it does not, the replay is broken and no row means anything.
FAIR RULE GAP is the headline: cone vs a generative head on the SAME lifted
   features with the SAME per-class-only information. The old cone-vs-rp_ridge
   comparison was naive-Bayes vs LDA and always flattered RanPAC.
NON-NEGATIVITY is the foundational test: `sub` is a rank-R subspace at IDENTICAL
   R*d storage, so cone - sub isolates w>=0 and nothing else. <= 0 means the
   conic parameterisation earns nothing over a plain span.
LDA is rank-limited to n_seen-1, so early stages are structurally starved. That is
   a real property of LDA in CIL, not an artifact -- read A-Avg, not just A-Last.
Sweep NROWS=5,10,20,50,0 for the regime axis. CUB200 has 27 rows/class and
   ImageNet-A 18, so the low-NROWS rows predict those datasets directly.
