READ `inactive` FIRST. If the constraint is inactive on most (q,c) pairs the
   cone IS the subspace there and no accuracy comparison between them measures
   anything -- exp38's -0.10 would be a null result, not a negative one.
`differential` is the only quantity that can change an argmax: a constraint that
   shaves the same amount off every class is a constant. Read it against
   `margin`; differential/margin is the fraction of a decision it can move.
`disagree` bounds the whole question empirically: sub and cone can differ on at
   most that many queries, so |cone-sub| accuracy is capped by it.
